{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q21009595","formula":"C₁₅H₁₈N₂","hill":"C15H18N2","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":18.0,"N":2.0},"names":{"en":"N-isopropyl-N'-phenyl-1,4-phenylenediamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"N-Isopropyl-N′-phenyl-1,4-phenylenediamine (often abbreviated IPPD) is an organic compound commonly used as an antiozonant in rubbers. Like other p-phenylenediamine-based antiozonants it works by virtue of its low ionization energy, which allows it to react with ozone faster than ozone will react with rubber. This reaction converts it to the corresponding aminoxyl radical (R2N–O•), with the ozone being converted to a hydroperoxyl radical (HOO•), these species can then be scavenged by other antioxidant polymer stabilizers."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":7573,"mass":226.32,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)NC1=CC=C(C=C1)NC2=CC=CC=C2","inchikey":"OUBMGJOQLXMSNT-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-N-phenyl-4-N-propan-2-ylbenzene-1,4-diamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"7573","atoms":35,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.845,"y":0.341,"z":0.149,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.688,"y":1.248,"z":-0.034,"el":"N"},{"x":4.474,"y":-0.866,"z":-0.386,"el":"C"},{"x":2.488,"y":0.563,"z":0.105,"el":"C"},{"x":4.315,"y":-2.025,"z":0.594,"el":"C"},{"x":5.946,"y":-0.588,"z":-0.671,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.297,"y":1.02,"z":0.012,"el":"C"},{"x":1.922,"y":1.743,"z":0.636,"el":"C"},{"x":1.611,"y":-0.38,"z":-0.474,"el":"C"},{"x":0.546,"y":1.968,"z":0.59,"el":"C"},{"x":0.235,"y":-0.155,"z":-0.52,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.799,"y":0.381,"z":-0.017,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.979,"y":0.743,"z":-0.669,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.721,"y":-0.842,"z":0.652,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.078,"y":-0.115,"z":-0.652,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.821,"y":-1.7,"z":0.669,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.999,"y":-1.337,"z":0.017,"el":"C"},{"x":4.032,"y":-1.136,"z":-1.353,"el"